        "currentWorkarounds": [
          "Text editors (unstructured, no organization, all notes open at once)",
          "Google Keep (not structured enough for PM work)",
          "Separate paid to-do list apps (fragmented from notes, costs money)"
        ],
        "frequencySeverity": "Daily — every meeting, every planning session. Costs ~5 hours/day per PM in context-switching, searching, and fragmented tool usage. Leads to missed action items, lost context, and blocked execution.",
        "oneLiner": "Product Managers waste 5 hours a day because they lack a single structured tool to think, plan, write, and track — forcing them into fragmented, unstructured apps that cost money and lose context."
