      "source": "user-input",
      "data": {
        "oneLiner": "A free, lightweight markdown app that unifies notes, to-do lists, and kanban boards in a single workspace — purpose-built for how PMs think, plan, and track work.",
        "keyCapabilities": [
          "Markdown notes with rich editing",
          "To-do lists with sub-tasks and descriptions",
          "Kanban board to move and manage note cards",
          "Visual notes tree — editable, draggable hierarchy",
          "Search, tags, and bi-directional linking",
          "Templates for common PM workflows",
          "Offline support — works without internet"
        ],
        "differentiation": "Competitors like Notion are powerful but bloated and expensive. Obsidian is markdown-native but lacks built-in kanban and task management. Todoist handles to-dos but not notes. This app is the only free, lightweight tool that combines all three — notes, tasks, and kanban — without the complexity or cost.",
        "magicMoment": "A PM finishes a meeting, captures notes in markdown, checks off action items as to-dos, drags a card onto their kanban board — all without leaving the app or paying a dime. One tool. Zero friction.",
        "customerQuote": {
          "quote": "I used to juggle Google Keep, Todoist, and a folder full of text files. Now everything lives in one place — my notes, my tasks, my board. I stopped paying for three apps and I'm actually more organized.",
